Ok so things went really well for me.  I found the entrance to the
mines on lvl4, but I went off to do sokaban first.  I ended up
defeating 4 Wraiths all of them left corpses.  So I had four extra
levels.  I found a couple of wands of magic missle and three wands of
lightning.  I found some nice enchanted armor items as well as
gauntlets of power.  So by the time I finished sokaban and returned to
the mines, I was lvl 12 (almost 13) with an AC of 1.  I also had two
large dogs and a housecat.  This is the best I've been going into the
mines.  I had not found an alter yet, and only had a collection of
daggers, throwing stars, and my quarterstaff for weapons.

The mines were rather easy, although I had to flee a couple of times
when some solider ants joined with some killer bees and surrounded me.
Lucikily I was near the stairs and could flee and rest for a little
while (In the heat of the moment I forgot about the E-word).  I make it
to minetown as lvl 14.  My pets basically clear out the guards for me.


The alter is neutral and I'm chaotic.  Well that needs to change.  Of
course I need to take out that priest first.  So I line up and zap him
with lightning.  Somehow I get zaped by a booming voice down to 1hp.  I
of course flee the level.  I come back the priest is still peaceufl.
So I try my magic missle wand. Oh same thing happens.  Returning a
third time I wonder if it is because my beam hit the alter both times,
so I try a different position and zap the priest again.  Again the same
thing happens, only this time the priest moves in and hits me before I
can get out and I die.

So WTF happened?  The only time I've ever been able to kill the priest
and convert the alter is when I had a wand of death.  I know from past
experience that you've got to kill the priest before converting the
alter, otherwise they get a couple of free hits and kill you.



